# AFC Church Portal — staging Caddy with rate_limit module (AFC-1217).
#
# Stock `caddy:2-alpine` has no `rate_limit` directive: uncommenting the
# `register` zone in services/staging/Caddyfile against stock breaks the
# ingress. This image adds exactly one module and nothing else.
#
# Module choice: github.com/mholt/caddy-ratelimit (512★, canonical).
# Its Caddyfile shape matches the commented zone verbatim —
#   rate_limit { zone <name> { match { method … path … }
#                window <dur> events <n> } }
# — and excess answers 429 with a Retry-After header (handler.go:
# rateLimitExceeded). No other candidate was closer; generic forward-auth or
# stock `request_header` hacks cannot keep per-IP sliding-window state, so
# they were rejected (see services/staging/README.md §9).
#
# Pins (exact — do not float):
#   CADDY_VERSION=2.10.0  (matches the module's go.mod requirement;
#     builder and final image stay on the same minor)
#   MODULE_VERSION=5625512f24f6f59d6f64fb3aafe5eecff0b286db
#     (upstream master 2026-06-12, "fix(metrics): re-register collectors
#     on each config reload (#102)"). Only published tag is v0.1.0
#     (2024-08-28, caddy v2.8.0 era); master is pinned by SHA because the
#     zone shape plus Retry-After already exist at v0.1.0 but the pinned
#     revision carries two years of fixes on the exact Caddy minor below.
#
# Per-IP key note: the zone sets `key {remote_host}` (README Caddyfile
# placeholder form of {http.request.remote.host}). Without a key the module
# keeps ONE global bucket for the whole zone — that would cap open day at
# 20 registrations/min TOTAL, contradicting the contract doc §5
# ("20 events/min/client IP"). The key is the one-line deviation from the
# AFC-1210 commented shape, stated here, not silent.
#
# Cloudflare caveat: TLS terminates at Cloudflare Flexible (AFC-561), so
# RemoteAddr at origin is Cloudflare edge unless trusted_proxies /
# X-Forwarded-For handling is added later. The key still partitions edge
# IPs; true per-client partitioning behind the proxy is a CTO follow-up,
# not this image.
#
# Build (VPS): docker compose -f services/staging/compose.yml build caddy
# Rollback: stock `caddy:2-alpine` line kept commented in compose.yml —
#   comment the build block, uncomment the stock line, keep the zone
#   commented, re-run up. No postgres/Directus changes; no new ports.

ARG CADDY_VERSION=2.10.0
ARG MODULE_VERSION=5625512f24f6f59d6f64fb3aafe5eecff0b286db

FROM caddy:${CADDY_VERSION}-builder-alpine AS builder
ARG CADDY_VERSION
ARG MODULE_VERSION
RUN xcaddy build v2.10.0 \
  --with github.com/mholt/caddy-ratelimit@${MODULE_VERSION}

FROM caddy:${CADDY_VERSION}-alpine
COPY --from=builder /usr/bin/caddy /usr/bin/caddy
